{title: Surrender}
{song_number: 168}
{language: en}
{tempo: 66}
{comment: Marc James}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[E]I'm giving You my heart and [B]all that is within.
[A]I lay it all down [B]for the [C#m]sake of You, my King.
[E]I'm giving You my dreams, [B]I'm laying down my rights;
[A]I'm giving up my [B]pride [C#m]for the promise of new [E]life.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[E]I'm singing You this song, I'm [B]waiting at the cross,
[A]and all the world holds [B]dear [C#m]I count it all as loss
[E]for the sake of knowing You, [B]the glory of Your name,
[A]to know the lasting [B]joy, [C#m]even sharing in Your [E]pain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C#m]And I sur[B]render all to [E]You,
[A]all to [E]You.
[C#m]And I sur[B]render all to [E]You,
[A]all to [E]You.
{end_of_chorus}
